# Local JSON-storage runtime database (users, sessions/refresh tokens, scan history, etc.).
# Previously committed with a live admin refresh token and hardcoded default admin password --
# see audit/new.md CRITICAL SEC-01. Never re-track this file; if it needs to be inspected, read it
# locally, never `git add` it. Regenerated automatically on first boot via ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD.
figm-user-db.json

# Real-world benchmark: third-party repos cloned by run-real-world-benchmark.ts. Never commit
# other projects' source code -- only our own scan output (benchmarks/real-world/raw-results/)
# and reports are tracked.
benchmarks/real-world/.repo-clones/

# Developer/audit scratch directory: ad-hoc probe scripts, captured live tokens/cookies, JSON
# response dumps from manual testing sessions. This directory has repeatedly accumulated files
# containing live JWT access/refresh tokens (see audit/ULTIMATE_FINAL_FORENSIC_AUDIT.md, finding
# HIGH-SCRATCH) -- exactly the class of artifact the figm-user-db.json incident above already
# proved is dangerous to leave a single `git add -A` away from being committed. Never re-track it.
scratch/

# VS Code extension compiled build output -- regenerate via `npm run compile` (vscode-extension/,
# `tsc -p ./`) from tracked src/. Same class of generated artifact as the root project's own
# .next/dist/build above; was previously (and unnecessarily) checked in as 152 tracked files (see
# audit/ULTIMATE_FINAL_FORENSIC_AUDIT.md, finding LOW-VSCODEBUILD).
vscode-extension/out/
